ient with key ID\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"new CryptographyClient(keyId, this.credential) where keyId is the full key identifier URL from key.id.\"},{\"name\":\"CryptographyClient for wrapKey/unwrapKey\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"cryptographyClient.wrapKey() and cryptographyClient.unwrapKey() used correctly.\"},{\"name\":\"Specifies RSA key wrap algorithm\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Uses 'RSA-OAEP-256' as the KeyWrapAlgorithm constant.\"},{\"name\":\"Key material never leaves Key Vault\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Only wrap/unwrap operations performed via CryptographyClient — vault key material stays server-side.\"},{\"name\":\"Generates random AES-256 DEK locally (32 bytes)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"randomBytes(32) generates a 32-byte (256-bit) DEK locally. dataKeyLengthBytes = 32.\"},{\"name\":\"Encrypts data with AES-GCM locally using DEK\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"createCipheriv('aes-256-gcm', plaintextKey, iv) used for local encryption.\"},{\"name\":\"Wraps DEK via Key Vault wrapKey()\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"cryptographyClient.wrapKey(wrapAlgorithm, plaintextKey) wraps the DEK server-side.\"},{\"name\":\"Stores wrapped DEK in blob metadata (base64)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"wrappedKey.toString('base64') stored in metadata under 'wrappeddek' key.\"},{\"name\":\"Stores IV in blob metadata (base64)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"iv.toString('base64') stored in metadata under 'iv' key.\"},{\"name\":\"Stores GCM auth tag in blob metadata (base64)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"authTag.toString('base64') stored in metadata under 'authtag' key — correctly handles Node.js separate auth tag.\"},{\"name\":\"Stores vault key identifier in blob metadata\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"keyId stored in metadata under 'keyid' key.\"},{\"name\":\"Decryption: retrieves wrapped DEK, unwraps, setAuthTag, decrypts\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Downloads blob, reads metadata, unwraps DEK via unwrapKey(), calls decipher.setAuthTag() before decipher.update()/final().\"},{\"name\":\"Uses AES-GCM (not CBC/ECB)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"CONTENT_ENCRYPTION_ALGORITHM = 'aes-256-gcm' used consistently for both encrypt and decrypt.\"},{\"name\":\"Random IV per encryption (12 bytes for GCM)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"randomBytes(IV_LENGTH_BYTES) where IV_LENGTH_BYTES = 12, generated fresh per uploadBuffer call.\"},{\"name\":\"Retrieves auth tag via cipher.getAuthTag()\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"cipher.getAuthTag() called after cipher.final() to retrieve the authentication tag.\"},{\"name\":\"Sets auth tag via decipher.setAuthTag()\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"decipher.setAuthTag(Buffer.from(authTagBase64, 'base64')) called before decipher.update().\"},{\"name\":\"Handles Key Vault errors via RestError\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Key Vault errors are caught as generic errors and re-wrapped. No RestError import, no statusCode inspection for key-disabled or key-not-found cases.\"},{\"name\":\"Handles Storage errors via RestError with statusCode\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Uses blobClient.exists() for 404 detection instead of catching RestError with statusCode 404. Other storage errors caught generically without RestError type checking.\"},{\"name\":\"NOT using SecretClient\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"No SecretClient import or usage anywhere in the codebase.\"},{\"name\":\"NOT encrypting data directly with vault key\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Envelope encryption pattern: DEK encrypts data locally, vault only wraps/unwraps the DEK.\"},{\"name\":\"NOT storing raw DEK in plaintext\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Only the wrapped (encrypted) DEK is stored in blob metadata. Plaintext DEK is ephemeral in memory.\"},{\"name\":\"NOT omitting GCM auth tag from metadata\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Auth tag explicitly stored in metadata as 'authtag' and used during decryption via setAuthTag().\"}]},\"overall_score\":36,\"max_score\":40,\"summary\":\"Excellent implementation of envelope encryption with Azure Key Vault Keys and Blob Storage. The code correctly implements all cryptographic patterns (AES-GCM with separate auth tag, 12-byte IV, 32-byte DEK, RSA-OAEP-256 key wrapping), uses the correct Azure SDK packages with latest versions, and has clean architecture with proper separation of concerns. The four failures are: (1) no RestError type-checking for Key Vault errors, (2) no RestError type-checking for Storage errors (uses exists() instead), (3) no @azure/logger usage, and (4) the general RestError criterion. These are all observability/error-handling refinements rather than correctness issues.\",\"issues\":[\"No RestError import or statusCode inspection — all Azure service errors caught as generic Error and re-wrapped with cause chain. Should import RestError from @azure/core-rest-pipeline and check statusCode for specific handling (e.g., 403 key disabled, 404 blob not found).\",\"No @azure/logger integration — should import setLogLevel from @azure/logger or reference AZURE_LOG_LEVEL for SDK diagnostic logging.\",\"Uses blobClient.exists() before download instead of catching 404 RestError — exists() requires an extra network call and is a less idiomatic pattern.\",\"credential parameter typed as ManagedIdentityCredential instead of TokenCredential — reduces flexibility for testing and alternative auth scenarios.\"],\"strengths\":[\"Correct use of @azure/keyvault-keys with KeyClient + CryptographyClient (not SecretClient)\",\"Proper envelope encryption: local AES-256-GCM encryption with KV-wrapped DEK\",\"All cryptographic metadata (wrapped DEK, IV, auth tag, key ID, algorithm) stored in blob metadata as base64\",\"Correct Node.js AES-GCM pattern: separate getAuthTag()/setAuthTag() handling, 12-byte IV, 32-byte DEK\",\"Latest Azure SDK package versions verified via npm registry\",\"Clean architecture with config, key manager, encrypted blob storage, and demo entry point\",\"Shared ManagedIdentityCredential instance across all clients\",\"Robust error wrapping with Error cause chains for debugging\"]}"
